<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ryazan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pereyaslavl-Ryazansky</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ryazan is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> on the Oka river, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. Called Pereyaslavl-Ryazansky until 1778, it replaced Old Ryazan, destroyed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> in 1237, as the seat of the princes of Ryazan in the fourteenth century. The principality was annexed by Moscow in 1521, and the city keeps its kremlin with the Dormition Cathedral.</p></div>
